  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to consider the geometry and the distances between the points on the cube. Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the coordinates of the points on the cube:**\n   - Each dot is at the midpoint of a square on one of the faces of the cube.\n   - The cube has 6 faces, and each face is a square with side length 6 cm.\n   - The dots are placed at the midpoints of the sides of each face, so the coordinates of the dots on one face can be represented as \\((x, y, 0)\\) where \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) range from 0 to 6 in increments of 3 (since the dots are at the midpoints).\n\n2. **Calculate the distance between two points:**\n   - The distance between two points \\((x_1, y_1, z_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2, z_2)\\) in 3D space is given by the formula:\n     \\[\n     d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2 + (z_2 - z_1)^2}\n     \\]\n   - Since the dots are on the same face and at the midpoints, the distance between any two dots on the same face is the same as the distance between the midpoints of two adjacent sides of the square.\n\n3. **Calculate the distance between two dots on the same face:**\n   - For example, the distance between the dot at \\((0, 0, 0)\\) and the dot at \\((3, 3, 0)\\) is:\n     \\[\n     d = \\sqrt{(3 - 0)^2 + (3 - 0)^2 + (0 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 9} = \\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - This is the distance between two dots on the same face.\n\n4. **Calculate the total length of all the line segments:**\n   - There are 9 dots on each face, and each dot is connected to 8 other dots (since it is not connected to itself and the dots directly adjacent to it).\n   - Therefore, each face has \\(9 \\times 8 / 2 = 36\\) line segments (since each segment is counted twice).\n   - Since there are 6 faces, the total number of line segments is \\(6 \\times 36 = 216\\).\n   - The total length of all the line segments is \\(216 \\times 3\\sqrt{2} = 648\\sqrt{2}\\) cm.\n\n5. **Calculate the numerical value:**\n   - The value of \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) is approximately 1.414.\n   - Therefore, \\(648\\sqrt{2} \\approx 648 \\times 1.414 = 912.312\\) cm.\n   - Rounding 912.312 to the nearest whole number gives us 912 cm.\n\nSo, the total length of the line segments is \\(\\boxed{912}\\) cm.",
